      "message": "Give reading an allowance too\n\nWrites have had one since agents started retrying them; reads had none,\nand reads are what a stranger can ask for without an account. A clone\nis the expensive one — it forks git and streams a pack — and nothing\nabout being anonymous made it cheaper.\n\nWhoever is asking decides whose allowance is spent: a principal when\nthe request carries identity, resolved the way each door resolves it,\nand the source address otherwise. Two allowances rather than one, so a\nbusy agent cannot use up what everybody else has and a stranger cannot\nuse up what people with accounts have. Running out is 429 with\nRetry-After, the shape a write already refuses with. Assets and the\nhealth check are not counted, because a monitor polling the forge to\nsay whether it is up should never be the thing that runs out.\n\nWith this the list of what a forge on the open internet has no defence\nagainst is one line shorter, and the guide now says plainly what is an\nowner's and what is the operator's on a forge somebody else runs — and\nthat leaving needs no export button, because it is all git and the\nreceipts verify off the forge.\n\nChange-Id: Ireads0100\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
